# Backend (Django + DRF)

## Apps

Work inside `kiosk_backend/apps/` — accounts, products, orders, payment, admin_panel, core, bale_bot, logs.

## API conventions

- DRF viewsets/APIViews with existing URL prefixes (`/api/kiosk/...`)
- Auth: SimpleJWT Bearer tokens for admin; public endpoints stay public
- Prefer serializers + permissions already used in the same app
- OpenAPI via drf-spectacular — keep schema-friendly serializers when practical
- Pagination/filtering: django-filter patterns already in project

## ORM & performance

- Avoid N+1: use `select_related` / `prefetch_related` on list and nested responses
- Add DB indexes when filtering/ordering new fields heavily
- Do not put secrets or hardcoded credentials in settings; use env via dotenv/compose

## Domain notes

- Orders + payment integrate with POS/card flows — preserve transaction/status semantics
- Receipt printing and Persian text shaping (arabic-reshaper / bidi) may be involved; do not break encoding
- Admin panel APIs under `/kiosk/admin/...` power the Next admin UI

## Agent tooling

- Use Context7 for Django/DRF version-accurate docs when unsure
- Use Postman MCP (if authenticated) against the OpenAPI/collection rather than inventing endpoints
